## Summary
Indian National Security Adviser Ajit Doval visited China for border talks with Foreign Minister Wang Yi. During the visit, he also discussed bilateral relations with Chinese Vice President Han Zheng, focusing on border issues and diplomatic engagement.

## Key Points
- Indian NSA Ajit Doval is holding border talks in China with Foreign Minister Wang Yi.
- The talks aim to address ongoing border disputes between India and China.
- Doval met with Vice President Han Zheng to discuss broader bilateral relations.
- This meeting reflects diplomatic efforts to enhance India-China relations.
- Discussions likely cover security cooperation and regional stability.


